WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.168
-Today,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.270
today was Donald Trump's
last full day

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.939
as president
of the United States

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.640
and he spent it stewing
in private,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.542
mulling pardons
for well-connected allies

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.478
and releasing a meaningless,
lie-filled farewell message.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.814
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:18.784
♪♪

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:21.221
Today, Trump released
a pretaped farewell message

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:24.189
filled, as usual, with the
soaring oratory he's known for.

00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:25.391
-My fellow Am--
-[Bleep] off.

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:26.926
You don't get to do that.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.561
You don't want to do any
of the hard parts of leaving,

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.096
like gracefully
admitting you lost

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.831
and attending
your successor's inauguration,

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.466
but you want us to watch
your lie-filled

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.900
20-minute farewell speech,

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.068
which, I am certain,

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:37.469
you're reading
for the first time,

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:40.439
like a tourist reading a menu
in a foreign language.

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:42.241
[ As Trump ]
I'll -- I'll have the --
Oh, boy.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:44.577
Oh, how do you say this?

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.379
Oh, man!

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.381
Oh. Hamburger?

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.782
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:52.619
Although, I will briefly touch
on the overarching message

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.253
because of how absurd it is.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:57.790
-Four years ago, we launched
a great national effort

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:01.227
to rebuild our country,
to renew its spirit,

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.095
and to restore the allegiance

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:05.798
of this government
to its citizens.

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:11.804
We did what we came here
to do, and so much more.

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:14.007
-[ As Trump ]
And, yet, sadly,
my presidency ends

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:18.010
one week
before Infrastructure Week.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.380
Are you insane?
You left the nation in ruins.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.181
What did you come here to do,
wreck the economy;

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:24.918
spread disease; and take selfies
with cans of beans,

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:28.187
where you smile like you just
ate ice cream with a cavity?

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:29.288
This time, four years ago,

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:30.756
virtually the entire
federal government

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:33.926
was being mobilized in service
of an incredibly stupid lie --

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.995
Trump's insistence
that his inauguration crowd

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.398
was the largest ever,
even though we could all see

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.799
that it had more white space

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.701
than the back
of a Hallmark card.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.369 line:0%
Sean Spicer was screaming
from the podium

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.305 line:0%
in a giant suit cut

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.407 line:0%
from the sail
of a mighty clipper ship.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.909 line:0%
Trump was whining in front
of the CIA Memorial Wall.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:52.912 line:0%
Kellyanne Conway was trying
to Jedi mind trick Chuck Todd

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.480 line:0%
into accepting alternate facts.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.482 line:0%
And that episode ended up
being a telling preamble

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:57.950
to the rest of Trump's
four years.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.919
It's not just
that Trump inhabits

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.854
an unhinged fantasy world,
which he does,

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.724
or that he and his aides lie
as easily as they breathe,

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.058
which they do.

00:02:06.058 --> 00:02:09.195
It's that the entire
federal bureaucracy was dragged

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:12.164
into defending a narcissistic
president's delusion

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:15.134
and anyone who refused
to support the lie was punished.

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.102
-Newly released documents
obtained by The Guardian

00:02:17.102 --> 00:02:20.473
reveal a government photographer
intentionally cropped the images

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:24.110 line:15%
to remove spaces and, in turn,
make the crowd look larger.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:27.780 line:15%
The unnamed photographer says
that he tampered with the photos

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.149 line:15%
from the president's
inauguration in 2017

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:32.751 line:15%
after receiving multiple calls
from the White House,

00:02:32.751 --> 00:02:35.455 line:15%
including one from the president
on his first full day in office.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:38.624 line:15%
-The president, here,
reportedly asking

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:40.793 line:15%
for additional pictures
of the inauguration.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:41.927 line:14%
He was obviously concerned

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:44.363 line:15%
about the crowd size
of the inauguration.

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:47.166 line:15%
The request appeared to have
trickled down to other members,

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:49.335 line:15%
other staffers
at the Park Service,

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:52.171 line:15%
one unnamed official
telling investigators

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.073 line:15%
with the
Inspector General's Office

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.743 line:15%
that she got the impression
that the president wanted to see

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:59.779 line:15%
pictures that appeared to depict
more spectators in the crowd.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:02.615
-That's right. Trump bullied
the National Park Service.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:03.683
First of all,
if you're going to make

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.618
the National Park Service
edit photographs,

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:09.222
at least make it something fun,
like Old Faithful spewing lava

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:13.259
or a moose
with Angelina Jolie's eyes.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.760
Good-looking moose!

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.495
And, as we've learned
over the last four years,

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:19.031
if you're willing to lie
about inconsequential things,

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:21.067
like crowd size
or a weather map,

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:24.103
you're also willing to lie
about far more important things,

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.571
like the coronavirus pandemic,

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:29.041
which has now passed a grim
new death toll of 400,000

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:30.543
on Trump's final day in office.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.812
Trump insisted that COVID
would magically disappear,

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.314
that it could be easily cured,

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:35.782
and, much like
the inauguration lie,

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.683
everyone around him,
from his closest aides

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.385
to government scientists,
was ordered

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.654
to fall in line
or face consequences.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.690
And, while some stood up to him,
his closest sycophants decided

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:48.093
to take part in the lie
and deny reality.

00:03:48.093 --> 00:03:51.431
-You have 15 people and the 15,
within a couple of days,

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:53.766
is going to be
down to close to zero.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.434
It's going to disappear one day.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.470
It's like a miracle.
It will disappear.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.272 line:8%
-We've actually contained
the spread of this virus.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:02.041
It is being contained. And --

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.542
Do you not think
it's being contained?

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:06.612
-So far, it looks
relatively contained

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:07.880 line:8%
and we don't think
most people --

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.782 line:8%
I mean, the vast majority
of Americans

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.650 line:8%
are not at risk
for this virus.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.453 line:8%
-People don't die
of this disease anymore.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.887 line:7%
-I went through the CDC data

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:17.056 line:8%
because I kept hearing
about new infections,

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:19.324 line:8%
but I was like, "Well, why
aren't they talking about this?

00:04:19.324 --> 00:04:21.761 line:8%
Oh, oh, because the number
is almost nothing."

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.863
-Oh, you went
through the CDC data?

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:27.032
I have a hard time imagining
Don Jr. staying up all night,

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:28.568
sifting through graphs
and charts,

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:31.770
although he does have the manic
energy of a guy with a head mic

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.639
selling time-shares
in Boca Raton.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:34.807
[ As Don Jr. ]
I went through all the data

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:37.209
and you can vacation,
anytime you want,

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:39.278
for a fraction of the price,
and, plus,

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:41.480
you'll be long dead
before global warming

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:44.884
sinks your condo like a castle
in an aquarium. Whoo!

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:47.252
And then, of course, there were
Trump's poisonous lies

00:04:47.252 --> 00:04:49.655
about the election,
indulged and echoed

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.857
by the vast majority
of the Republican Party

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:53.292
and right-wing media apparatus,

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:56.194
which led to the deadly
insurrection at the Capitol.

00:04:56.194 --> 00:04:59.131
Anyone who has watched Trump
for the last four years

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:01.834
should not have been shocked
and, today, Mitch McConnell,

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.636
in his last day
as Senate majority leader,

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.038
finally laid the blame
at Trump's feet.

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:08.875
-The mob was fed lies.

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:10.209
They were provoked

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.276
by the president

00:05:11.276 --> 00:05:14.113
and other powerful people.

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.881
-First of all,
some of those powerful people

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:17.183
are in your caucus.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.484
If you really mean
what you're saying,

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:19.985
then you can start
by expelling them.

00:05:19.985 --> 00:05:21.621
Hawley can go back to starring

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:23.322
in his Patrick Bateman
miniseries

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:26.125
and Cruz can be remembered
as Bigfoot Danny Zuko.

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:28.327
Second, I'm glad
you're finally coming around,

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:29.695
but it's four years too late.

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:31.197
You made your bargain
with the devil,

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.931
to get your judges and tax cuts,

00:05:32.931 --> 00:05:35.000
and, now, much like
a Stephen King character

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.936
who hits a drifter with your car
and buries him in the wood,

00:05:37.936 --> 00:05:40.973
you will be cursed forever
with a frog's voice.

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.508
Well, for you, you know,
obviously,

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.544
it will have to be
a different curse, but,

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:45.711
you know, you get the idea.

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:48.814
[ As McConnell ]
Oh, tough break, drifter.

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:50.183
I already got that.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:51.851
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.418
So this is the legacy
Trump will leave behind,

00:05:53.418 --> 00:05:55.954
one of insurrection,
corruption, cruelty, and chaos,

00:05:55.954 --> 00:05:58.624
and, as a result, he'll leave
as the most unpopular president

00:05:58.624 --> 00:05:59.858
in modern American history.

00:05:59.858 --> 00:06:02.327
Now, when Trump entered office
four years ago,

00:06:02.327 --> 00:06:04.863
he was already the most disliked
incoming president

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:06.098
in the history of polling.

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:07.800
He lost the popular vote
by three million;

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.668
he never cracked 50% approval;

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:12.838 line:0%
and, in a bit of foreshadowing,
the stands at his inauguration

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:16.109 line:0%
were emptier than the D Train
at 3:00 am during a pandemic.

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:17.743
And, yet, as he's preparing

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:19.344
to leave office
four years later,

00:06:19.344 --> 00:06:23.048
he's somehow even more unpopular
than when he first started.

00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:24.750
The last Gallup poll
of his presidency

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.285
put his approval at 34%,

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:28.754
and the last Pew poll
put it at 29%,

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:30.423
both the lowest numbers

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:32.191
he's ever recorded
in either one of those polls.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.493
Usually, presidents' approval
ratings tick up when they leave,

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:35.594
and, yet, Trump is leaving

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:37.363
with the lowest ratings
of his presidency

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.264
and the lowest ratings
to end any first term

00:06:39.264 --> 00:06:41.733
in the history of polling,
but I found this number

00:06:41.733 --> 00:06:43.169
to be the most damning...

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.876
Not only do people hate him
and want him out,

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:52.110
but a full two-thirds
of Americans

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:53.245
want him gone forever.

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:55.047
Basically,
the entire country has turned

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:56.515
into Trump's guidance counselor.

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:58.951
"Now, it says here
you want a future in politics,

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:01.086
but, have you considered

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:03.488
yelling at birds in the park?

00:07:03.488 --> 00:07:05.391
So Trump won't get
a stately retirement filled

00:07:05.391 --> 00:07:06.425
with events and honors.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:07.926
He won't even get
a quiet retirement.

00:07:07.926 --> 00:07:09.495
He'll have to deal
with an impeachment trial

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:11.096
in the Senate
that could disqualify him

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:12.398
from holding office ever again.

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:15.034
His neighbors don't want him
to move to Mar-a-Lago.

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:18.003
New York City canceled all
of its contracts with Trump.

00:07:18.003 --> 00:07:20.439
The D.A. in Atlanta is
considering investigating Trump

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:22.341
for his phone call
to Georgia election officials.

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:25.378
The Manhattan district attorney
just subpoenaed more records

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:27.947
in his investigation of Trump,
and his advisors

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:30.483
and warned him that he could
face potential civil liability

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:31.817
for his role
in the insurrection.

00:07:31.817 --> 00:07:33.519
Trump is also spending
the last few hours

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:34.987
of his disastrous presidency

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:36.989
weighing pardons
for well-connected criminals,

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:39.725
which has created a lucrative
market for access to Trump

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:41.527
and lined the pockets
of his allies.

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:43.028
-The New York Times
reports that some

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:45.130
of Trump's friends and advisors
are collecting

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:49.302 line:8%
tens of thousands of dollars
from people seeking pardons.

00:07:49.302 --> 00:07:51.503 line:8%
Those who have access
to the president,

00:07:51.503 --> 00:07:52.972 line:7%
his longtime aides,

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:55.140 line:8%
as well as some former attorneys
who have worked for him,

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:58.510 line:8%
have essentially been peddling
their access to the president

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:00.145 line:7%
to try to bring in money

00:08:00.145 --> 00:08:02.715 line:8%
from convicted felons
who want a pardon.

00:08:02.715 --> 00:08:04.216 line:7%
Associates of the president,

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:07.052 line:8%
allies as well as attorneys who
have worked for him in the past,

00:08:07.052 --> 00:08:09.588 line:8%
have been collecting
these lucrative fees

00:08:09.588 --> 00:08:11.991 line:8%
from people trying
to seek these pardons,

00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:14.193 line:7%
involving, at least in one case,

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:17.162 line:8%
a report to the FBI
about allegations

00:08:17.162 --> 00:08:18.965 line:8%
that Rudy Giuliani
might have been trying

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:21.901 line:7%
to essentially sell a pardon for

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:25.337 line:8%
what The New York Times reports
was a $2 million fee.

00:08:25.337 --> 00:08:27.173
-That's right,
Rudy Giuliani reportedly tried

00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:28.908
to sell a pardon for $2 million.

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:31.577
Even worse,
he did it via bus stop ad.

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.045
[ Laughter ]
Honestly, though,

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:34.280
that's the only thing
that makes me

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.581
even slightly suspicious
of this story --

00:08:36.581 --> 00:08:37.816
Rudy didn't advertise.

00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:39.051
You think he'd be
going door to door,

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:40.586
asking people
if they committed a crime

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:41.587
or he'd be on Fox News,

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:43.756 line:0%
selling pardons like it was QVC.

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:46.859 line:0%
Of course, this is how
the Trump era ends,

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:49.228
with the faux populist president
mulling pardons

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:51.263
for wealthy,
well-connected allies.

00:08:51.263 --> 00:08:53.132
He's already used his pardon
and clemency powers

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:55.701
to help out accomplices
and close friends,

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.336
like Roger Stone, Paul Manafort,

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:59.538
Michael Flynn,
and Jared Kushner's dad.

00:08:59.538 --> 00:09:00.906
In one of his most heinous acts,

00:09:00.906 --> 00:09:02.741
he pardoned four
Blackwater mercenaries

00:09:02.741 --> 00:09:05.110
convicted of murdering
innocent Iraqis.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:08.281
And, yet, even with Trump
considering up to 100 pardons,

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:09.715
there's one guy
in his inner circle

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:11.517
who reportedly
can't get a pardon,

00:09:11.517 --> 00:09:13.085
and he sounds
a little peeved about it.

00:09:44.983 --> 00:09:47.186
[ Laughter ]
That was Rudy's radio show.

00:09:47.186 --> 00:09:48.286
Or, at least, I think it was.

00:09:48.286 --> 00:09:49.721
It could just as easily
have been

00:09:49.721 --> 00:09:51.157
at the drive-through
at McDonald's.

00:10:04.837 --> 00:10:10.009
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:13.378
So Rudy spent five years
debasing himself

00:10:13.378 --> 00:10:15.814
in service of Trump,
a man with no proven loyalty,

00:10:15.814 --> 00:10:18.084 line:0%
who is reportedly considering
a pardon of Lil Wayne,

00:10:18.084 --> 00:10:20.085 line:0%
which I'm assuming cost a milli,

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:21.386 line:0%
and, yet,
Rudy can't get a pardon.

00:10:21.386 --> 00:10:25.825
Rudy, I hate to even ask,
but have you considered rapping?

00:10:25.825 --> 00:10:28.327
[ As Giuliani ]
♪ My name is Rudy
and I'm here to say ♪

00:10:28.327 --> 00:10:30.129
♪ I totally forgot
what I'm here to say ♪

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:32.031
[ Laughter ]

00:10:32.031 --> 00:10:34.066
Honestly, there's a better
chance, at this point,

00:10:34.066 --> 00:10:35.467
that Trump turns him in.

00:10:35.467 --> 00:10:36.668
[ As Trump ]
Hello, FBI?

00:10:36.668 --> 00:10:40.405
Yeah, I want to report
a guy who incited a riot.

00:10:40.405 --> 00:10:42.341
Yeah, he's also one
of those dead voters

00:10:42.341 --> 00:10:43.342
I've been hearing about.

00:10:43.342 --> 00:10:45.611
Just stay over there, Rudy.

00:10:45.611 --> 00:10:46.979
Have some tea.

00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:48.113
[ Laughter ]

00:10:48.113 --> 00:10:49.815
In fact, Rudy,
a loyal Trump ally

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:51.283
who has stood by him
through everything,

00:10:51.283 --> 00:10:52.718
can't get a pardon and, yet,

00:10:52.718 --> 00:10:55.253
Trump is reportedly considering
a pardon for a former ally

00:10:55.253 --> 00:10:57.089
who left his administration
in disgrace

00:10:57.089 --> 00:10:59.858
and got arrested for trying
to con Trump's own supporters.

00:10:59.858 --> 00:11:01.893 line:15%
-CNN has learned the president
was back in touch

00:11:01.893 --> 00:11:03.662 line:15%
with his former strategist
Steve Bannon,

00:11:03.662 --> 00:11:06.131 line:15%
discussing Trump's
election conspiracy theories.

00:11:06.131 --> 00:11:08.800 line:8%
Sources say Bannon, who's facing
federal fraud charges,

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.602 line:14%
is seeking a pardon from Trump.

00:11:10.602 --> 00:11:12.805
-That's right, Bannon wants
a pardon, for, I'm guessing,

00:11:12.805 --> 00:11:14.940
bursting
out of that dude's chest.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.075
And, if you think Kuato's
too fringe a reference,

00:11:17.075 --> 00:11:18.711
take it up with Andy Samberg,

00:11:18.711 --> 00:11:21.213
who fully played him
in a sketch.

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:22.581
Chill, Quaid.
You'll get your Smint.

00:11:22.581 --> 00:11:23.782
So Bannon wants a pardon

00:11:23.782 --> 00:11:25.183
for scamming
Trump's own supporters

00:11:25.183 --> 00:11:27.252
by raising money
for a private border wall

00:11:27.252 --> 00:11:30.189
that allegedly skimmed
about a million bucks

00:11:30.189 --> 00:11:31.656
for his own personal expenses.

00:11:31.656 --> 00:11:33.358
In fact, if you'll recall,

00:11:33.358 --> 00:11:35.127
Bannon,
the self-proclaimed populist...

00:11:42.634 --> 00:11:44.402
Was he on the yacht

00:11:44.402 --> 00:11:47.406
or did they find him
getting dragged behind it?

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:48.407
I mean, look at him.
He looks like

00:11:48.407 --> 00:11:51.109
a waterlogged baked potato.

00:11:51.109 --> 00:11:54.312
He looks like Jimmy Buffett
two weeks after he drowned.

00:11:54.312 --> 00:11:56.515
"We found the body wasting away

00:11:56.515 --> 00:11:57.550
in Margaritaville."

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.618
[ Laughter ]

00:11:59.618 --> 00:12:00.786
But we have to remember that,

00:12:00.786 --> 00:12:02.988
even as disgraced
and unpopular as Trump is today,

00:12:02.988 --> 00:12:05.457
there are still powerful forces
in the Republican Party

00:12:05.457 --> 00:12:07.393
and the right-wing
media ecosystem

00:12:07.393 --> 00:12:08.661
who will try to memory-hole

00:12:08.661 --> 00:12:10.228
what happened
these last four years,

00:12:10.228 --> 00:12:13.532
and they'll go to absurd,
humiliating lengths to do it.

00:12:13.532 --> 00:12:15.233
Lindsey Graham said this weekend

00:12:15.233 --> 00:12:16.902
he wants Trump
to keep his movement alive

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:18.703
and remain the leader
of the Republican Party.

00:12:18.703 --> 00:12:19.872
And then there's
the Fox &amp; Friends,

00:12:19.872 --> 00:12:22.007
who insisted today that,
despite Trump spending

00:12:22.007 --> 00:12:24.577
more time and taxpayer money
at his private properties

00:12:24.577 --> 00:12:28.413
than any president in history,
actually worked super hard.

00:12:28.413 --> 00:12:30.116
-They'll criticize
President Trump,

00:12:30.116 --> 00:12:32.684 line:15%
but no one can argue
he is a worker.

00:12:32.684 --> 00:12:34.619 line:15%
You know,
he doesn't drink alcohol.

00:12:34.619 --> 00:12:36.254 line:14%
He stays up late at night.

00:12:36.254 --> 00:12:37.690 line:14%
He watches every show.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.259 line:15%
He's working.
He got to work immediately.

00:12:40.259 --> 00:12:41.927
-Your evidence
that he's a hard worker

00:12:41.927 --> 00:12:43.929
is that he watches every show?

00:12:43.929 --> 00:12:46.231
Is he the president
or the editor of TV Guide?

00:12:46.231 --> 00:12:48.400
You sound like a spouse
defending her deadbeat husband

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.802
who refuses to look for work.

00:12:49.802 --> 00:12:51.303
"Just because he's not
updating his résumé

00:12:51.303 --> 00:12:52.604
doesn't mean
he's not working hard.

00:12:52.604 --> 00:12:53.872
He watches every show!

00:12:53.872 --> 00:12:55.941
'Price Is Right,' 'Maury.'

00:12:55.941 --> 00:12:58.410
All the soap operas,
which counts as research

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.612
because he's applying
to be an evil twin.

00:13:00.612 --> 00:13:01.981
He just got the eyepatch."

00:13:01.981 --> 00:13:04.283
The toxic right-wing
media apparatus

00:13:04.283 --> 00:13:06.285
and most of the institutional
Republican Party

00:13:06.285 --> 00:13:09.288
spent the last four years
colluding with a monstrous

00:13:09.288 --> 00:13:12.958
and irredeemable man who has
been thoroughly repudiated

00:13:12.958 --> 00:13:15.760
by the American electorate,
over and over and over again.

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:17.463
He lost the popular vote
in 2016;

00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:19.531
lost the House
by a record margin in 2018;

00:13:19.531 --> 00:13:20.966
got impeached;
lost the presidency

00:13:20.966 --> 00:13:23.034
by 7 million votes in 2020;

00:13:23.034 --> 00:13:24.436
lost the Senate in 2021,

00:13:24.436 --> 00:13:26.872
including two seats
in a longtime red state;

00:13:26.872 --> 00:13:28.373
and then got impeached again.

00:13:28.373 --> 00:13:30.309
You know what? I take it back.
Maybe he is a worker,

00:13:30.309 --> 00:13:33.679
because you have to work pretty
hard to be this unpopular.

00:13:33.679 --> 00:13:35.581
If Trump had spent
four years golfing,

00:13:35.581 --> 00:13:37.449
ranting about low-flush toilets,

00:13:37.449 --> 00:13:39.784
and letting the experts
do their job,

00:13:39.784 --> 00:13:41.286
there'd be a good chance
he'd be setting off

00:13:41.286 --> 00:13:42.721
for a retirement
of paid speeches

00:13:42.721 --> 00:13:44.590
and toilet endorsement deals.

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.224
[ As Trump ]
Introducing the super flusher.

00:13:46.224 --> 00:13:48.493
This baby roars
like a jet engine

00:13:48.493 --> 00:13:50.896
and it sucks down anything
you put in it --

00:13:50.896 --> 00:13:52.231
number one, number two,

00:13:52.231 --> 00:13:54.600
subpoenas, tax returns,
you name it.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.401
Here, let's give it a whirl.

00:13:56.401 --> 00:13:59.538
[ Creak, toilet flushes,
jet engine whines ]

00:13:59.538 --> 00:14:00.539
Oh, God!

00:14:00.539 --> 00:14:02.074
Oh, God. Mel?!

00:14:02.074 --> 00:14:04.542
[ Laughter ]
Mel!

00:14:04.542 --> 00:14:06.011
Did you get flu-- Oh!

00:14:06.011 --> 00:14:07.346
Oh, there you are, Mel.

00:14:07.346 --> 00:14:08.447
[ As Melania ]
I'm right here, Donald.

00:14:08.447 --> 00:14:10.482
[ As Trump ]
Oh, I was so worried, Mel.

00:14:10.482 --> 00:14:11.483
Worried sick.

00:14:11.483 --> 00:14:12.684
After all we've been through,

00:14:12.684 --> 00:14:14.453
if I lost you like that, Mel,

00:14:14.453 --> 00:14:15.921
oh, I couldn't have beared it.

00:14:15.921 --> 00:14:18.690
I mean, I would've married
pretty quickly.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:20.092
Have my eye
on a couple of candidates,

00:14:20.092 --> 00:14:21.927
but I would've been sad, Mel.

00:14:21.927 --> 00:14:24.363
So sad.
No crying sad.

00:14:24.363 --> 00:14:25.731
But I wouldn't have smiled,

00:14:25.731 --> 00:14:27.166
even though,
"sucked down a toilet,"

00:14:27.166 --> 00:14:29.901
it's a pretty funny way to go,
you have to admit that, Mel.

00:14:29.901 --> 00:14:32.070
Now, show me
that million-dollar smile

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:34.139
I've never seen once.

00:14:34.139 --> 00:14:36.041
Instead, Trump will go
down in history

00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:37.809
as a disgraced,
sadistic con artist

00:14:37.809 --> 00:14:39.078
who left the nation in ruins.

00:14:39.078 --> 00:14:40.345
He's less popular than Bush,

00:14:40.345 --> 00:14:41.746
he's broken more laws
than Nixon,

00:14:41.746 --> 00:14:43.882
he's got a worse jobs record
than Hoover,

00:14:43.882 --> 00:14:46.618
and he leans like a house
blown over in a storm

00:14:46.618 --> 00:14:48.721
that Jimmy Carter
would have to fix.

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:49.721
[ As Carter ]
We're going to do our best,

00:14:49.721 --> 00:14:52.257
but the problems
in the foundation.

00:14:52.257 --> 00:14:53.558
See?
We're going to be fine.

00:14:53.558 --> 00:14:55.260
I got Carter.

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:57.729
[ Laughter ]

00:14:57.729 --> 00:14:59.331
And, as he leaves,
he'll be remembered,

00:14:59.331 --> 00:15:02.201
not for standing by the people
he pretended he would help.

00:15:02.201 --> 00:15:04.469
Our economy is in tatters,
hospitals are overrun,

00:15:04.469 --> 00:15:06.204
and the vaccine rollout
is a disaster.

00:15:06.204 --> 00:15:09.575
He'll be remembered for standing
by people like Charles Kushner,

00:15:09.575 --> 00:15:11.509
Paul Manafort; Steve Bannon;

00:15:11.509 --> 00:15:13.278
murderous
Blackwater mercenaries;

00:15:13.278 --> 00:15:15.480
and the MyPillow guy,
who, it should be noted,

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:18.416
is now facing a possible lawsuit
for his election lies

00:15:18.416 --> 00:15:21.353
and whose products are being
dropped by major retailers.

00:15:21.353 --> 00:15:25.356 line:15%
-Lindell has repeatedly claimed
the 2020 election was a fraud.

00:15:25.356 --> 00:15:27.559 line:8%
Last week, he was seen
leaving the White House

00:15:27.559 --> 00:15:29.294 line:14%
with some notes and documents,

00:15:29.294 --> 00:15:32.264 line:15%
with all kinds of conspiracies
along those lines.

00:15:32.264 --> 00:15:33.632 line:14%
Dominion Voting Systems

00:15:33.632 --> 00:15:35.967 line:15%
has also sent a cease
and desist letter to Lindell

00:15:35.967 --> 00:15:39.204 line:15%
over his spread of lies
related to the election.

00:15:39.204 --> 00:15:41.840 line:15%
-MyPillow products
will no longer be sold

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:43.775 line:14%
by some big-name retailers.

00:15:43.775 --> 00:15:46.645 line:14%
MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell says

00:15:46.645 --> 00:15:49.882 line:15%
that several companies
are dropping his products

00:15:49.882 --> 00:15:52.718 line:15%
because he is a supporter
of President Trump.

00:15:52.718 --> 00:15:54.019 line:14%
Bed Bath &amp; Beyond,

00:15:54.019 --> 00:15:56.889 line:8%
Kohl's, and Wayfair are
among the companies

00:15:56.889 --> 00:15:59.124 line:14%
that have cut ties with Lindell.

00:15:59.124 --> 00:16:00.892
-[ Laughs ]
He was too beyond

00:16:00.892 --> 00:16:02.327
on for Bed Bath &amp; Beyond.

00:16:02.327 --> 00:16:04.796
That's like when Rudy found out
he was too nuts

00:16:04.796 --> 00:16:06.899
for Chock full o' Nuts.
Hey-o!

00:16:06.899 --> 00:16:08.967
[ Laughter ]

00:16:08.967 --> 00:16:12.137
You get it.
Shoemaker likes it.

00:16:12.137 --> 00:16:14.005
And, yet, the president
repeatedly invited him

00:16:14.005 --> 00:16:15.440
into the White House,
anyway, to share

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:18.309
his deranged election lies
and scam coronavirus cures.

00:16:18.309 --> 00:16:19.878
And, by the way,
even in the face

00:16:19.878 --> 00:16:23.214
of a lawsuit and lost business,
Lindell still can't offer

00:16:23.214 --> 00:16:24.883
any proof
for his conspiracy theories.

00:16:24.883 --> 00:16:27.252
For example, in an email
to NBC News, Lindell said...

00:16:46.171 --> 00:16:48.507
We've all pulled that move, when
you're behind on a work project

00:16:48.507 --> 00:16:50.009
and your boss wants
to see a draft,

00:16:50.009 --> 00:16:51.876
so you pretend
your email isn't working.

00:16:51.876 --> 00:16:53.378
Here it is.
"Hm, that's weird.

00:16:53.378 --> 00:16:54.579
The attachment
didn't go through.

00:16:54.579 --> 00:16:56.281
Can you try again?"
Sure! Look at this!

00:16:56.281 --> 00:16:57.683
"That's just a picture
of your thumb."

00:16:57.683 --> 00:16:59.217
Oh, no, my laptop.

00:16:59.217 --> 00:17:00.785
I must've flushed it
down the toilet.

00:17:00.785 --> 00:17:04.923
[ Creak, toilet flushes,
jet engine whines ]

00:17:04.923 --> 00:17:06.692
[ As Trump ]
Mel! Oh, there you are.

00:17:06.692 --> 00:17:08.993
[ Laughter ]

00:17:08.993 --> 00:17:10.863
The Trump presidency
may be drawing to a close,

00:17:10.863 --> 00:17:12.263
but the dysfunction,
the corruption,

00:17:12.263 --> 00:17:14.066
the authoritarianism,
an the moral rot

00:17:14.066 --> 00:17:17.202
Trump exposed within the GOP
and in our system will remain,

00:17:17.202 --> 00:17:19.638
and we can't just let it go.
We've got to fix it.

00:17:19.638 --> 00:17:21.974
We have to hold accountable
the people responsible for it,

00:17:21.974 --> 00:17:23.575
from the top
all the way down.

00:17:23.575 --> 00:17:25.777
Otherwise,
this four-year-long nightmare

00:17:25.777 --> 00:17:28.113
we've all lived through
could very well happen again.

00:17:28.113 --> 00:17:29.581
And, as for Trump,
when historians

00:17:29.581 --> 00:17:31.683
count his accomplishments,
they'll find that...

00:17:31.683 --> 00:17:33.619 line:14%
-The number is almost nothing.

00:17:33.619 --> 00:17:35.320
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:39.190
♪♪

00:17:39.190 --> 00:17:40.692
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:17:40.692 --> 00:17:42.060
